{"login": "loziogigio", "location": null, "commits": [{"sha": "4a9bdf2513ed3c843ebc6e27bd068b1caa006687", "message": "remove rate tenant", "created_at": "2025-11-11T15:09:48Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "810f7efde832dab7c0bdb0320c6ecbe62bb93544", "message": "Isolation Fixes", "created_at": "2025-11-11T07:31:02Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "24c262154b105b105daca371dfa9356c1dbf8d6f", "message": "CRITICAL: fix connection pool sharing with singleton pattern\n\nProblem Found:\n- Configurations() was instantiated multiple times per request\n- Each new instance created NEW connection pool (3+5 connections)\n- If 5 repositories used in one request = 5 pools = 40 connections!\n- Connection pool limits were PER-INSTANCE, not per-tenant\n- Completely defeated the purpose of pool limits\n\nRoot Cause:\n- Every Configurations() call created new instance\n- hasattr(self, 'mysql_connection') always False for new instance\n- Database() created fresh pool every time\n\nSolution - Singleton Pattern:\n- get_configurations_instance(): Cache instance per site\n- Connection pools now SHARED across all requests for same tenant\n- Pool limits (3+5) now work as intended per-tenant\n- B2BBaseRepository updated to use singleton\n\nImpact:\nBefore: 10 repository instances = 10 pools = 80 connections\nAfter: 10 repository instances = 1 shared pool = 8 connections \u2705\n\nThis fix is CRITICAL for connection pool limits to work correctly!", "created_at": "2025-11-11T05:41:51Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "10d6bcfae695cb3f9a4b18f21ec84e703e4e7e13", "message": "add per-tenant concurrent request limiting for complete isolation\n\nFinal layer of multi-tenant isolation to prevent worker monopolization.\n\nProblem:\n- 10 tenants share 8-10 gunicorn workers\n- Tenant with high traffic or slow operations can use all workers\n- Other 9 tenants must wait, causing slowness for everyone\n- Even with circuit breakers and timeouts, slow requests (29s) still block workers\n\nSolution - Per-Tenant Request Limits:\n- Each tenant limited to 3 concurrent requests (configurable)\n- If limit exceeded, request fails with HTTP 429 immediately\n- Workers freed for other tenants\n- Fair resource distribution across all 10 tenants\n\nNew Files:\n- TenantRateLimiter.py: Core rate limiting logic with cache-based tracking\n- request_hooks.py: Frappe before/after request hooks\n- TENANT_RATE_LIMITING.md: Complete documentation and configuration guide\n\nChanges:\n- hooks.py: Enable before_request and after_request hooks\n- Database.py: Add MySQL lock timeout (3s) and max query time (30s)\n\nConfiguration:\n- Default: 3 concurrent requests per tenant\n- Customizable per-tenant or per-endpoint\n- Monitoring API endpoint included\n\nImpact:\n- Tenant A with 10 concurrent requests \u2192 Only uses 3 workers\n- Remaining 5-7 workers available for other 9 tenants\n- Complete tenant isolation achieved", "created_at": "2025-11-10T05:49:21Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8f840c1bee0a17dd5d0e6882f0b74bce08343006", "message": "add circuit breaker pattern for multi-tenant isolation\n\nPrevents one tenant's slow/failing API or DB operations from blocking all tenants.\n\nProblem:\n- Shared worker pool = one tenant's 120s B2B DB timeout blocks all sites\n- No isolation between tenants sharing same backend infrastructure\n\nSolution - Circuit Breaker Pattern:\n- Tracks failures per API/DB endpoint\n- Opens circuit after 3 failures (fails fast, no blocking)\n- Auto-recovers after 30-60s timeout period\n- Prevents cascading failures across tenants\n\nChanges:\n- Add CircuitBreaker utility class with CLOSED/OPEN/HALF_OPEN states\n- Wrap all external API calls (MymbAPIClient, APIClient) with circuit breaker\n- Wrap B2B DB connections with circuit breaker\n- Reduce default DB pool size (3 base, 5 overflow) for all tenants\n- Add per-tenant connection pool limits\n\nImpact:\n- One tenant's failing B2B service won't block other tenants\n- Failed requests fail in <3s instead of hanging for 120s\n- Better resource isolation between tenants", "created_at": "2025-11-10T05:33:41Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "9d2d52376a70d70e62138418c82f2485b16e1070", "message": "email send changed end point", "created_at": "2025-10-27T10:24:53Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c882f5afdb863e3550451a84fb0642e3cbf2b446", "message": "fix B2B database connection timeouts to prevent worker blocking\n\n- Add 3s connection timeout to fail fast when B2B DB is unreachable\n- Add 30s read/write timeouts for query operations\n- Enable connection pooling with health checks (pool_pre_ping)\n- Add error handling and logging for connection failures\n\nFixes: Workers hanging for 120s on slow B2B connections (26% timeout rate)", "created_at": "2025-10-27T10:19:21Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c5c8af3342cb4576937fb18fcd93b7b745348652", "message": "improve API error handling and media repository filtering\n\n- Add media_area_id filter to MediaRepository (images/image only)\n- Reduce connection timeout from 30s to 3s for faster failure detection\n- Add explicit ConnectionError handling with email notifications\n- Implement email rate limiting (1 email per error type per 30min) to prevent spam\n- Apply improvements to both MymbAPIClient and APIClient", "created_at": "2025-10-27T05:15:05Z", "repo": "mymb_ecommerce", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d2e204f201798b2453487609d5e53d338e39229a", "message": "added category banner image", "crea